reconcile: fix forEach prune flake — per-node applied key tracking (#228)

## Summary

- Fix ~10% flake in `TestRGDLifecyclePort` where forEach scale-down
(N→0) fails to prune the removed child's Deployment
- Replace append-only `walkState.appliedKeys []string` with `nodeKeys
map[string][]string` (per-node, last-writer-wins)
- When a node is processed twice in the same walk (skip at Step 1, then
dispatch after propagation trigger), the second write overwrites the
first — stale carry-forward keys no longer cancel prune candidates

## Root Cause

`tryDispatch` runs the skip check (Step 1) before the dependency check.
When `rgd` is skipped, it dispatches dependents including
`instanceGraphs`. If `instanceGraphs` is not yet triggered, Step 1 fires
and `carryForwardKeys` appends the stale L2 Graph key to `appliedKeys`.
Later, when `instances` completes with a changed hash, `instanceGraphs`
gets a propagation trigger and dispatches — returning 0 keys (instance
deleted). But `appliedKeys` already has the stale key from the earlier
carry-forward. The prune phase sees both, and the stale key prevents
cleanup.

## Fix

`nodeKeys map[string][]string` — keyed by node ID, last writer wins.
Both `carryForwardKeys` and dispatch result processing write to
`nodeKeys[nodeID]`. After the walk, flatten into `appliedKeys` for the
prune phase. ~10 lines changed, no new abstractions.

## Validation

- `make presubmit` passes (vet, race, e2e, compat)
- `TestRGDLifecyclePort`: 20/20 passes (was ~9/10)
- All benchmarks pass with no regression
